Z||000014||MinnGreenGT||10-10-2001||04:32 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cliff Pennock:<BR><B>Skitime, I think you are using PIP, and if you do, there's no need to upload the same pic every time you want to use it in a message. To re-use an earlier uploaded picture, click on the "History" button of PIP, find the image, and click on the button directly below the image. This will save me [b]a lot</B> of diskspace. I've noticed you've uploaded this picture <B>13</B> times already!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> And the way PIP works, it will not overwrite an earlier uploaded version, but create a new one.[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Cliff- related question.  If I upload a picture with a title the same as another picture someone else has uploaded- when I write in code for it, it uses their photo (1st loaded photo)  ...but what happened to the one with the same name that I just uploaded?  Does it get a default extended name (like name_1.jpg)? Example... I uploaded a picture with "extrator1.jpg" or something similiar to it and someone else's pic posted when I used it- so I altered the name to "extrator1b.jpg" and reloaded it, which then of course worked fine.  Does this make sense?<P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
