Z||000017||Cliff Pennock||10-10-2001||04:48 PM||||MinnGreenGT, if you upload the same pic twice, or if you upload a pic with a name that already exists, PIP will automatically rename your pic on my server. For instance, if you upload a picture called <B>fiero.jpg</B>, and the forum already has a pic with that name, it will automatically be renamed to <B>fiero_1.jpg</B>. If that name already exists, it will be renamed to <B>fiero_2.jpg</B> etc. If you look at your history, you will see these names.<P>Skitime, just insert <B>any</B> floppy disk in your drive, click <B>History</B>, find the image(s) that came from your A: drive, and click the little button with the red circle directly below the image.||||reg||1
Z||000018||skitime||10-10-2001||05:06 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cliff Pennock:<BR>[Skitime, just insert <B>any</B> floppy disk in your drive, click <B>History</B>, find the image(s) that came from your A: drive, and click the little button with the red circle directly below the image.[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Gee thanks Cliff.  I never noticed those buttons or tried it with a floppy disk in the drive.  Now I can start cleaning the history files.<P>||||reg||1
